\title{LibeRties: portable execution for LibeR jobs}
\description{
Executes serialized LibeR simulation and estimation jobs in restricted subprocesses, hardened transient systemd user services, or resource-managed Slurm and Grid Engine allocations with isolated per-user working directories. A persistent cross-platform local queue uses background R worker processes and the same versioned job contract used by remote Linux servers. Payload checksums, explicit state transitions, metadata locking, safe path components, cancellation, logs, restart recovery, per-tenant quotas, monitored resource limits, and result provenance are built into the contract. Production deployments use the native systemd isolation backend or an independently attested scheduler sandbox and require TLS termination. A fixed typed-JSON SSH entry point also permits a desktop client to use a personal Slurm or Grid Engine account directly, including through an SSH gateway, without an HTTP daemon.
